    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling lineup anchored by **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (72.88) and **Jacob Wilson** (69.83), both of whom capitalize on favorable matchups against middling arms in hitter-friendly environments. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** faces a 4.53 xERA starter, and while the dynamic platoon splits are slightly negative, his raw base projection and batting order security make him our premier offensive engine. **Jacob Wilson** presents an even stronger opportunity, benefiting from a massive 10% park boost; his efficiency remains elevated due to a 4.68 xERA opposing starter and a favorable #4 hole assignment. **Andy Pages** (67.66) and **Sam Antonacci** (63.14) round out our top-tier plays, with **Andy Pages** gaining extra value from a slow-delivering opposing pitcher that provides a tangible bump for our team-wide focus on stolen bases.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today's roster was leaving **Miguel Vargas** (61.26) on the bench. He posted a strong score that easily cleared the \"Strong\" start threshold, but he ultimately ceded his spot to **Nolan Schanuel** (62.14) and **Josh Jung** (61.51), both of whom leveraged slightly better park factors or superior lineup protection to edge him out by the slimmest of margins. Managers should exercise caution regarding **Cole Carrigg** (50.00); while he has strong park factors, he is effectively dead-ended against an elite arm in Skenes. Similarly, **Gunnar Henderson** (62.29) is a must-start due to his profile, but be aware that his score is suppressed by facing Yamamoto, a premier SP who limits damage despite the potential for stolen base opportunities. Ensure your game caps are monitored closely, as we are prioritizing high-floor production over risky pivots like **Jackson Merrill** (49.41) or **Nasim Nunez** (45.92) while facing tough left-handed opposition.",
